      {
        "id": "p24-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Calculate, correct to two decimal places, the mean and standard deviation for each set of marks.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Mathematics: $\\bar{x}=16.13$, $\\sigma=2.63$.\n\nEnglish: $\\bar{x}=15.87$, $\\sigma=2.83$.",
          "worked": "Use the population standard deviation, dividing by $15$.\n\nMathematics:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\bar{x}_{M}&=\\frac{242}{15}\\\\\\bar{x}_{M}&\\approx16.13\\\\\\sigma_M&=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\sum(x_i-242/15)^2}{15}}\\\\\\sigma_M&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1556}{225}}\\\\\\sigma_M&\\approx2.63\\end{align*}$$\nEnglish:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\bar{x}_{E}&=\\frac{238}{15}\\\\\\bar{x}_{E}&\\approx15.87\\\\\\sigma_E&=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\sum(x_i-238/15)^2}{15}}\\\\\\sigma_E&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1796}{225}}\\\\\\sigma_E&\\approx2.83\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If a student scored 16 for the mathematics test and 14 for the English test, which is the better mark relative to the class results?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The mathematics mark is better: it is about $0.05$ standard deviations below its class mean, compared with about $0.66$ standard deviations below the English mean.",
          "worked": "Using the unrounded statistics from part a, compare the signed distances from the means in standard deviations:\n$$\\begin{align*}z_M&=\\frac{16-242/15}{\\sqrt{1556}/15}\\\\z_M&\\approx-0.05\\\\z_E&=\\frac{14-238/15}{\\sqrt{1796}/15}\\\\z_E&\\approx-0.66\\end{align*}$$\nThe mathematics mark is about $0.05$ standard deviations below its mean; the English mark is about $0.66$ standard deviations below its mean. The mathematics mark is better relative to the class results.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
